WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.705 --> 00:00:07.100
What happens in a chemical reaction?

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:11.380
Two products react with each other to form new products.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:18.760
To understand this in a simple way, we can say that A and B react together to give C and D.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:24.380
Two substances A and B reacted to give us two new substances C and D.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:27.820
This is a chemical equation.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:33.380
With the chemical equation, we´ll represent a chemical reaction with symbols.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.480
Clearly, there are two sides to this equation.

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:41.880
On the left, we have substances which take part in a chemical reaction.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.520
They are called reactants.

00:00:45.340 --> 00:00:49.800
And the new substances form after the reactions are called products.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.120
Reactants react to form products.

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:57.720
The arrow showed is the directions of the chemical reaction.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.100
A and B reacted to give us C and D.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.360
If there´s any condition it´s written above the arrow.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:10.380
For instance, if A and B reacted after heat was applied,

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.360
it will be written like this.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:15.020
To give you an example,

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:19.200
we know that hydrogen reacts with oxygen to give us water.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:24.060
As it´s a chemical change, it implies that a chemical reaction took place.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:28.900
Using words we can represent the chemical equation like this.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:31.240
Can we make it simpler?

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:35.680
Yes, we can use symbols off to substances to write the equation.

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.995
Hydrogen can be represented as H2,

00:01:39.995 --> 00:01:42.855
oxygen can be represented as O2,

00:01:42.915 --> 00:01:45.905
and water, as you know, is H2O.

00:01:46.055 --> 00:01:48.015
But look at this equation again.

00:01:48.345 --> 00:01:51.445
On the left, there are two atoms of oxygen.

00:01:51.445 --> 00:01:53.260
And at the right, there´s just one.

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:55.540
Where did the other one go?

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.260
It´s this chemical equation correct?

00:01:58.455 --> 00:02:00.295
Is there anything more we need to know

00:02:00.295 --> 00:02:03.105
about writing chemical equations?

00:02:03.105 --> 00:02:05.505
Keep watching our videos to know more.

